Source: asusctl
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cargo,
 rustc,
 pkgconf,
 libudev-dev,
 libusb-1.0-0-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenGamingCollective/asusctl
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: asusctl
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Control daemon and tools for ASUS ROG laptops
 asusd, a system daemon, and asusctl, its command-line client, control
 the features of ASUS ROG, TUF, Zephyrus and similar laptops: keyboard
 lighting (Aura), the AniMe and Slash LED displays, fan curves and power
 profiles, the battery charge limit, and panel overdrive. asusd starts
 from its own udev rule on the laptops it supports. asus-shutdown runs
 asusd's deferred shutdown tasks, and asusd-user keeps per-user
 lighting and display settings.
 .
 The @DISTRO_NAME@ installer installs this package on ASUS ROG laptops,
 and the desktop themes the keyboard lighting with it. The ROG Control
 Center GUI is not built.
